								<br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=765"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1386.msg13942#msg13942"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1386.msg13942#msg13942">Re: New Bitch Topic from Top Ten List</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #33 on:</b> January 26, 2005, 09:16:37 am &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							Garadan I am sure I can totally understand your point, being an ex guild leader of a small guild and having everyone come crying to you about everything. It is rather annoying and makes you feel more of a baby~sitter in a game you just want to have fun playing. It is a job more then fun and you tend to get to a point that you ask yourself about 50 times in an hour that you are actually logged on *is this shit worth this?* <br /><br />Now my personal view point is, it&#039;s not worth it, and that is why I stay away from guilds. It&#039;s not worth the petty whiners who claim *omgz you stole my lolly pop!* or the rejects who ninja loot. I have fun playing with a select few and I do not need ubah pixels to make my life happy in EQ. <br /><br />Was it shitty of Ascent to do what they did? Really it depends on your views I suppose. If you really don&#039;t want to deal with that end of the game IMHO get out of the high end raiding guilds. My opinion is your just pissed cause someone got your leet pixels. Everyone in the high end guild is there because they want something for themselves and really don&#039;t give a rats ass about anyone else. You can try to convince me otherwise,&nbsp; but I have seen too many people that I thought where the straight and narrow type do some shady shit. <br /><br /><br />People in EQ have gotten tired of being pushed around, pissed on, and just more or less screwed over by other players. That is why they have become such rejects in mass. I will admit, I have had a rep of being a bitch in the past. Did I give a shit? Not really because that is your opinion of me from a game and you really have no idea what type of person I am like in real life. Can I be moody? Sure, but then so can you so what is your point? <br /><br />There are too many other games out there for you to let this one get you down.
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" colspan="2" class="smalltext">
								</td>
							</tr><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
								</td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
									<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/ip.gif" alt="" border="0" /> Logged
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" /><div align="center"><br /><a href="http://www.magelo.com/eq_view_profile.html?num=847985" target="_blank"> <img src="http://home.mindspring.com/~jkocie/bb.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a> <br /><br />BUFF BISH<br />Moraganna Macabre<br />&quot;I don&#039;t know the the key to success, but the key to failure is trying to please everbody&quot;</div>
						</td>
					</tr>
				</table>
			</td></tr>
		</table>
	</td></tr>
