								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							<div class="quoteheader"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1386.msg13981#msg13981">Quote from: Callon on January 27, 2005, 01:40:14 pm</a></div><div class="quote">As for Time, well, sure a guild doesn&#039;t break any game rules by ignoring the rotation.  But when 3 guilds have a fair system worked out that avoids conflict with each other, and another guild comes in and ignores the arrangement, they&#039;re naturally going to piss off the first 3 guilds.  At that point they either care about being on good terms with other guilds or they don&#039;t.  If they care, they at least attempt to work something out that&#039;s agreeable to all.  If they don&#039;t, okay, but they shouldn&#039;t be surprised when others justifiably call them inconsiderate assholes.  </div><br />Honestly, atleast from the Era Ascent comes from.&nbsp; It doesn&#039;t matter if they didn&#039;t concern themselves with the rotation of other guilds.&nbsp; They got applicants cause they were the best and people wanted to be a part of that.<br /><br />Didn&#039;t matter if some folks thought they were assholes.&nbsp; Ascent still advanced because &quot;good&quot; players liked what they were capable of doing.&nbsp; <br /><br />Leasts thats the way I see successful guilds working.&nbsp; Oh I agree that there is a line that shouldn&#039;t be crossed when it comes to competition.&nbsp; But, I was just &quot;raised&quot; in the world of FCFS.&nbsp; Hard to see the game differently :P<br /><br />It&#039;s all sorta moot now anyways.&nbsp; I&#039;m waiting on Vanguard :P
						</td>
					</tr>
